<title>SINGAPORE: CAM says managing director resigns.</title>
<headline>CAM says managing director resigns.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>CAM International Holdings Ltd said on Friday it had accepted the resignation of its managing director and suspended another director pending investigations into an alleged fraud.</p>
<p>It said in a statement it had accepted the resignation of Raymond Chew Chuan Seng as managing director, and suspended Ng Chee Tiong from all his duties as group financial controller.</p>
<p>&quot;The company is still in the process of verifying the allegations,&quot; it said. &quot;The company will make further announcements as and when appropriate,&quot; it added.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
</text>
